ield keys would be removed and get a confirm_token, then call again with the same fields plus confirm_token to execute. If your new list drops any existing field you must ALSO pass allow_field_removal:true. Multi-step forms are not editable here. Requires form_id and fields.','Update Form Fields'=>'Update Form Fields','FluentForm context loaded. Use list-submissions and get-submission for entries, get-form-stats for per-form numbers.'=>'FluentForm context loaded. Use list-submissions and get-submission for entries, get-form-stats for per-form numbers.','Discovery'=>'Discovery','Get Forms Context'=>'Get Forms Context','An earlier attempt with this idempotency_key started but its outcome was never recorded, so it may or may not have completed. Check the current state before acting: if the change is already there, nothing more is needed; if it is not, retry with a NEW idempotency_key.'=>'An earlier attempt with this idempotency_key started but its outcome was never recorded, so it may or may not have completed. Check the current state before acting: if the change is already there, nothing more is needed; if it is not, retry with a NEW idempotency_key.','The record changed since you previewed it. Run a fresh dry_run to see the current state before executing.'=>'The record changed since you previewed it. Run a fresh dry_run to see the current state before executing.','The confirm_token does not match. Run a fresh dry_run.'=>'The confirm_token does not match. Run a fresh dry_run.','Your confirmation has expired. Run a fresh dry_run to preview and get a new confirm_token.'=>'Your confirmation has expired. Run a fresh dry_run to preview and get a new confirm_token.','START HERE — call once per session. Returns who you are and your permissions, the site info, every valid enum value (submission/form statuses), headline counts, a compact list of forms you can access (id, title, status, entries), and usage guidelines. Use this before any other tool so you never guess a status s